  "program": {
    "module": {
      "summary": "Corporation Tax Act 2010 s.18B — marginal relief for companies without\nring-fence profits.\n\nMarginal relief applies where augmented profits fall between the lower\nand upper limits, pro-rated by accounting-period length (`ap_year_fraction`,\na caller input so \"proportionately\" is not baked into the DSL) and by\n1 + the number of associated companies.\n\n  marginal_relief = F × (U_eff − A) × (N / A)\n\nF is the standard fraction (3/200 = 0.015). Main CT rate of 25% is\napplied to N outside this RuleSpec module; marginal relief reduces gross CT."
    },
